target/compiler-reference-capture-adoption-acceptance-1/report.md:3:Result: the two successful semantic publications account for **585 / 585 retained .lkj added+deleted lines** from language baseline 0b0b27803d27b932a5b91cde2d766bd3c8bb82b9. No uncovered source delta was found. This is source-publication attribution, not a new compiler/test execution or performance result.
target/compiler-reference-capture-adoption-acceptance-1/report.md:7:All **1,742** initial files under src/library/tests were independently checked against their exact baseline Git blobs. The core after manifest equals the test transaction before manifest byte-for-byte. All **1,743** final files match both the publication captures and current bytes. There are nine changed existing files and one new file; **1,733** original files remain unchanged.
target/compiler-reference-capture-adoption-acceptance-1/report.md:24:| Total | 24 | 23 | 10 | 585 |
target/compiler-reference-capture-adoption-acceptance-1/report.md:32:The source/library and all-retained-.lkj denominators are both 585 for this delta. The two host shell-tool edits are separate and add no .lkj lines. No refused/transient desired edits, whole-item source lengths, JSON/report/Rust/archive bytes or repeated validation copies are counted.
target/compiler-reference-capture-adoption-acceptance-1/report.md:56:acceptance.json is the immutable machine audit; projection-review.json records the subsequent complete hunk review. input-pins.json, baseline/live manifests, exact command records, raw stdout/stderr/time/status and all discrepancies are retained. One metadata inspection requested the nonexistent generic test numstat filename; its harmless missing-file diagnostic is retained separately. The actual audit independently recomputed numstat and used no missing record.
